## Testing and Validation

```java
import org.junit.jupiter.api.Test;
import static org.junit.jupiter.api.Assertions.*;

public class SessionSecurityTests {

    private SecureSessionManager sessionManager = new SecureSessionManager();

    @Test
    public void testRejectsSerializedPayloads() {
        String maliciousBase64 = "rO0ABXNyADJvcmcuYXBhY2hlLmNvbW1vbnMuY29sbGVjdGlvbnMubWFwLkxhenlN...";

        assertThrows(IllegalArgumentException.class, () -> {
            sessionManager.restoreSessionFromJsonSnapshot("test", maliciousBase64);
        });
    }

    @Test
    public void testAcceptsValidJsonSnapshot() throws Exception {
        String validJson = "{\"userId\":\"user123\",\"username\":\"john.doe\"}";

        assertDoesNotThrow(() -> {
            sessionManager.restoreSessionFromJsonSnapshot("test", validJson);
        });
    }

    @Test
    public void testRejectsInvalidFieldTypes() {
        String invalidJson = "{\"userId\":{\"nested\":\"object\"},\"username\":\"test\"}";

        assertThrows(IllegalArgumentException.class, () -> {
            sessionManager.restoreSessionFromJsonSnapshot("test", invalidJson);
        });
    }

    @Test
    public void testRejectsOversizedSnapshots() {
        String oversized = "{\"userId\":\"" + "a".repeat(11000) + "\"}";

        assertThrows(IllegalArgumentException.class, () -> {
            sessionManager.restoreSessionFromJsonSnapshot("test", oversized);
        });
    }
}
```

## Migration Checklist

✅ Replace `ObjectInputStream.readObject()` with JSON parsing
✅ Implement input validation for all session fields
✅ Whitelist allowed attributes and reject unknown ones
✅ Upgrade Spring Boot to 3.2.0+ (latest stable)
✅ Remove or upgrade commons-collections to 4.0+
✅ Implement deserialization filter for defense-in-depth
✅ Add OWASP dependency-check Maven plugin
✅ Set up attack detection filter
✅ Configure metrics and alerting
✅ Conduct security testing
✅ Perform penetration testing
✅ Update incident response procedures

## Key Differences: Serialization vs. JSON

| Aspect | Java Serialization | JSON Approach |
|--------|-------------------|---------------|
| **Security Risk** | Gadget chains, RCE | Type-safe, no code execution |
| **Performance** | Fast binary | Slightly slower text parsing |
| **Compatibility** | Version-dependent | Language-independent |
| **Debuggability** | Binary, opaque | Human-readable |
| **Attack Surface** | Massive (all classes) | Minimal (primitives only) |

The JSON-based approach eliminates the entire class of Java deserialization vulnerabilities while maintaining functionality and improving debuggability."
